WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.026 --> 00:00:05.580
- [Narrator] For the most
unique and ancient site

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:10.580
in all of Sri Lanka, you'll
need to look up, way, way up.

00:00:10.837 --> 00:00:14.087
(lively, bouncy music)

00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:21.110
Located 660 feet on top of a rock plateau

00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:24.150
in the Matale District of
Sri Lanka, lay the ruins

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:26.900
of a 5th Century fortress
of King Kashyapa.

00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:31.270
The shape and size of the rock
jutting out from the jungle

00:00:31.270 --> 00:00:35.450
below was created by hardened
lava from an extinct volcano,

00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:38.170
which dates back to prehistoric times.

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:40.150
The rock formation has come to be known

00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:43.140
by the name, Sigiriya, or Lion Rock,

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:45.900
after the large stone lion
that once marked the entrance

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:47.060
to the staircase.

00:00:48.550 --> 00:00:50.760
Visitors climbing to
the top should prepare

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:54.280
for the 1,200 steps it will
take to scale Sigiriya.

00:00:54.280 --> 00:00:56.960
To distract from the steep
climb, visitors can study

00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:00.820
the 1,500-year-old frescoes
painted all along the rocks.

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:05.310
At the top are the abandoned
remains of the King's fortress,

00:01:05.310 --> 00:01:07.840
along with an incredible view
of what are believed to be

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:10.560
some of the oldest landscaped
gardens in the world.

00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:13.630
It's a long climb, but once at the top,

00:01:13.630 --> 00:01:16.550
you'll be experiencing what
is referred to by locals

00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:18.280
as the 8th Wonder of the World.

00:01:23.926 --> 00:01:26.509
(bell chiming)

